<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nihawand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/642">642 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Victory of Victories · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-persia">Muslim conquest of Persia</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Nihawand was fought in 642 CE in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> between the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> and the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. Called the &quot;Victory of Victories&quot; in Islamic tradition, it effectively destroyed the remaining organised Sasanian military capacity. The battle opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a> to the Arab conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nihawand.jpg" alt="Battle of Nihawand" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eugène Flandin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castle_Nahavend_by_Eug%C3%A8ne_Flandin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Battle of Nihawand</b> in 642 CE, remembered in Islamic tradition as the “Victory of Victories”, broke the last organised Sasanian field army.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate · Military</a></li></ul></section>
